    <bpmn:process id="W_W3897" name="W3897. Customer 360 Consumption &amp; Self-Service Access" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Consumer need (marketing/sales/service); self-service request
Frequency: Continuous
Volume: ~100–300 entitled users; thousands of 360 lookups/day
Owner: CDP / Data Governance
Participants: CDP Team, Marketing (links to VS-14), Loyalty (links to VS-13), Sales Enablement/Clienteling (links to VS-124), Trade/Key Account (links to VS-11/VS-107), Contact Center (links to VS-13), Insights (links to VS-28.1), Privacy (links to VS-91), IT (links to VS-27)
Source: workflow W3897 — Customer 360 Consumption &amp; Self-Service Access</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3897_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3897_Lane1" name="CDP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3897_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3897_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3897_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3897_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3897_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3897_Start3" name="Consumer need (marketing/sales/service); self-service request">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3897_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3897_Task4" name="CDP publish the Customer 360 view for entitled consumers: contact-center agent…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: CDP publish the Customer 360 view for entitled consumers: contact-center agent screen-pop (links to VS-13), clienteling view at POS (links to VS-124/VS-08), key-account 360 (links to VS-107), marketing self-service segmentation (links to W3889), and trade-pro view (links to VS-43)
Responsible (R): CDP / IT / Data Governance
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3897_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3897_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3897_Task5" name="CDP/Privacy govern 360 access: role-based views, field-level masking of…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CDP/Privacy govern 360 access: role-based views, field-level masking of sensitive attributes (links to VS-91/W3888), purpose-limitation per consumer role, and audit logging of all lookups
Responsible (R): CDP / Privacy / Security
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3897_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3897_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3897_Task6" name="CDP/Insights train consumers and self-service adoption (links to VS-19.4/VS-124…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CDP/Insights train consumers and self-service adoption (links to VS-19.4/VS-124 enablement), monitor usage and value, and refine the 360 with consumer feedback
Responsible (R): CDP / Insights / Consumers
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3897_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3897_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3897_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3897_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3897_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-609 (ensure controlled execution — Customer 360 Consumption, Privacy &amp; Governance Analytics (PA-126.3).) | - operational: role-based views and masking (links to VS-91); operational: enablement and UX
Owner: CDP / Data Governance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3897_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3897_Annotation8" targetRef="W3897_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3897_Flow10" sourceRef="W3897_Start3" targetRef="W3897_Task4" />
