        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: CDP/Privacy run DPIA for new high-risk CDP processing (profiling/ML, identity resolution links to W3883, vendor data-sharing, biometric-adjacent data — links to VS-91/W389), and register with NPC where required
Responsible (R): CDP / Privacy / Legal
Accountable (A): CDP Lead / DPO
Duration: Per purpose</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3901_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3901_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3901_Task5" name="CDP/Privacy audit consent and processing against the records of processing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CDP/Privacy audit consent and processing against the records of processing (RoPA — links to VS-91): verify consent-at-ingestion (links to W3882), consent-at-activation (links to W3891), purpose-limitation, and cross-entity sharing (links to VS-72)
Responsible (R): CDP / Privacy / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): CDP Lead / DPO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3901_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3901_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3901_Task6" name="CDP/Privacy remediate findings, update the RoPA and notices (privacy policy…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CDP/Privacy remediate findings, update the RoPA and notices (privacy policy links to VS-91/VS-10/VS-75), and brief the privacy committee and Audit Committee (links to VS-21/VS-36)
Responsible (R): CDP / Privacy / Legal
Accountable (A): CDP Lead / DPO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3901_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3901_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
